{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_202609170635358f1659d929b04376","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"So the \"memory safety stop\" is the memWatch which calls `os.Exit(exitFailed)` when resident memory exceeds the threshold. Under the mandated 4GB cap, the Python lowering + graph construction over multi-package code exceeds it, so the scan dies before any finding is emitted.\n\nThe task says the fix should make the scan complete within 4GB / 180s so the repository scan can produce a report (specifically for rank 2794 which needs `razer_report_data_size_unclamped.vyql` — a C binding, probably on some repository with a large Python component, like... hmm, \"razer\" — maybe the target is a repository containing Python multi-package code plus C code).\n\nThe core issue: Python lowering and graph construction over multi-package code uses too much memory. So we need to find the memory hog in the Python path and reduce it.\n\nLet me look at the harness.log / harness.err in the worktree — those might contain evidence from the run that hit this.","signature":"2a1eb47a502144b3b32127a7"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"1fb99a01-9ad8-4fbc-a36f-9252c44be2be","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:35:40.270Z"}
