{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_2026091706361425fa0f90d09b4ecf","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The openrazer repository is the target: CVE-2022-23467 (`razer_report_data_size_unclamped`), CVE-2022-29021/29022/29023 — these are the classic OpenRazer buffer overflow CVEs (unclamped `razer_report` `data_size` in the Python daemon → crafted USB report allows buffer overflow in the C driver/daemon). Rank 2794 is presumably one of these — specifically `razer_report_data_size_unclamped.vyql` matches CVE-2022-23467 (out-of-bounds read, CWE-125).\n\nThe openrazer repo: the Python daemon (`daemon/` with many `razer_*` device modules — multi-package), `pylib/`, plus C in `driver/`. The scan lowers all the Python multi-package code, and graph construction exceeds 4GB.\n\nSo my job: reproduce the memory problem on openrazer, find the hog in the Python lowering/graph construction, and reduce it so the scan completes under the 4GB cap and 180s timeout.\n\nLet me check where the repo checkouts live — maybe there's a cached clone. Let me look at campaign-scan to understand what it does.","signature":"8d88512ab8d24d1c99324c75"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"ad5f85f6-928d-49b0-87e9-27b897d9d608","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:36:19.390Z"}
