{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260917063845e3da046371504557","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The heap profile is written via `onExit(...)` — the `runCleanups()` in memwatch's `onExceed` should run these (memwatch calls `runCleanups()` before `os.Exit`). Good: so even when the memory stop fires, the heap profile gets written.\n\nLet me run with `-memprofile` and no `-max-ram` cap (or a much bigger cap so it goes further and shows the real hog — actually with the blowup it would eat the machine's 31GB; better keep the 4GB cap so it stops at 3.3GB and dumps the heap at that point, which shows exactly what was accumulating).\n\nAlso a cpuprofile would show where time goes (13 minutes with ceiling raised).","signature":"2786acc51f44417187729f7e"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"f87db8ea-cd75-46ec-9513-4187def9f906","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:38:50.054Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260917063845e3da046371504557","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The heap profile flush is wired into the same cleanup path the memory stop runs, so I can capture the heap at the moment of the stop:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"8eb626e7-7a36-478b-b931-4897628e8fb8","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:38:50.055Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_20260917063845e3da046371504557","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"glm-5.3","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"call_3d3f852e56d74e5b96ba6420","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"timeout 170 ./bin/vyql scan -data /campaign/repos/defs -max-ram 4GB -cache off -memprofile /tmp/heap.prof /campaign/work/rank-2794-1/repo > /tmp/scan.out 2> /tmp/scan.err; echo \"exit=$?\"; cat /tmp/scan.err | head -5; ls -la /tmp/heap.prof","description":"Capture heap profile at memory stop","timeout":200000}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"e5f95f4c-6509-4c4b-bbdf-bee50a881a9d","timestamp":"2026-09-16T22:38:50.635Z"}
