{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   I am the \"engine gap\" role of a campaign adding CVE detections to the vyql scanner. The task file `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.task.json` names one gap: \"the engine's memory safety stop ends a whole-repository scan before any finding is emitted when the Python lowering and graph construction over multi-package code exceeds it, so under the mandated 4GB cap and 180 second timeout the repository scan writes an empty report and no rule's repository-level proof can be produced\" (blocked rank: 2794; branch `engine-work/the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan`). Explicit constraints:\n   - May change ONLY `internal/`, `cmd/`, `go.mod`, `go.sum`. No `vyql/` edits (definitions belong to ranks).\n   - The change must be the smallest that makes the behaviour expressible; must include a Go test that fails without the change and passes after; must be committed in this worktree only; must end by writing a verdict (parseable, every field checked) to `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.answer.json`.\n   - Must use `campaign-scan <target> --data-dir <dir>` (it enforces `timeout 180`, `--max-ram 4GB`, `--cache off`), never raw scanner runs on real repos.\n   - No merging; say blast radius plainly; three refusals park the gap; name blockers for what they are; \"Your work counts only committed\"; leftovers in the worktree are from dead runs (`git reset --hard && git clean -fd` is safe here only); never bare `git stash`.\n   - Commit attribution: end commit messages with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`; PR descriptions with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`.\n   - AGENTS.md repo rules: `go test -count=1` always; `CGO_ENABLED=1`; detection changes need benchmark numbers; reasoning goes in CHANGELOG.md and the PR, not README/RESULTS.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - vyql scanner architecture: extract (tree-sitter frontends) → NIR → lowering → USG graph (usg.Store) → binding application → rule evaluation; `pattern → concept → binding → rule` layering.\n   - Memory safety stop: `cmd/vyql/memwatch.go` — resident-memory sampler; `memoryStopThreshold(4GB)` = 3.5GB (displays \"3.3 GiB\"); on exceed → runCleanups + `os.Exit(1)` with empty report.\n   - `applyMaxRAM` (cmd/vyql/main.go): partitions budget, sets Go soft heap limit (`goHeapMemoryLimit`), sets `lowering.DiskStorePath` (→ disk-backed BadgerGraph), `DiskCacheBytes = clamp(n/16,…)` (256MB @4GB), `DiskDetailBuf = detailBufferBytes(n)` (512MB @4GB); fallback branch (unwritable cache dirs) sets `lowering.UseIntStore = true`.\n   - Store selection in `internal/extract/lowering/incremental.go` `newGraphStore`: `UseIntStore || DiskStorePath == \"\"` → `usg.NewIntStore`; else `usg.OpenBadgerGraphUnder`.\n   - Partitioning: `extract.PlanPartitions(paths, excludes, limit, budget)`; `oneGraphSourceBytes(4GB)` = 512MB/64 = 8MB JS-equivalent source; Python GraphWeight ≈ ×5; `scanPartitionsCollect` forces `UseIntStore=true` per partition (precedent for the fix).\n   - BadgerGraph vs IntStore: BadgerGraph keeps structural core in RAM + detail buffer (map, estimate-based spill) + badger write path/caches; IntStore holds everything in compact parallel slices.\n   - `campaign-scan` internals (python campaign.scan): `timeout 180 vyql scan -data <dir> --max-ram 4GB --cache off <target>`.\n   - Exit codes: 0 success, 1 could not complete, 3 check ran and did not pass.\n   - Go tooling: heap/CPU profiles via `-memprofile`/`-cpuprofile` (flushed even on memory stop via onExit cleanups), GODEBUG=gctrace=1, pprof.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.task.json` — the gap definition (read-only).\n   - `/campaign/work/rank-2794-1/verdict.json` + `task.json` — blocked rank's evidence: openrazer clone at fix 33aa7f07, parent 8f50fda, CVE-2022-23467; whole-clone scan blocked at the memory stop; clone left at repo/ (I used it read-only and removed the temporary worktree I added).\n   - `cmd/vyql/main.go` — **MODIFIED (the fix)**:\n     - `applyMaxRAM` doc comment updated to \"arms the disk-backed BadgerGraph store … (see holdOneGraphInRAM for when one that it can holds RAM instead)\".\n     - New helper after `minPartitionBytes`:\n       ```go\n       // holdOneGraphInRAM decides the store for a scan building ONE resident graph under a RAM\n       // ceiling, and returns the func that undoes its decision.\n       // … (comment documents: disk store costs more than the graph it spares for a target\n       // the ceiling holds — measured 4626MiB through the disk store against 1220MiB in RAM —\n       // and the safety stop ends the scan before the first rule has run …)\n       func holdOneGraphInRAM(paths []string, excludes extract.Excludes) func() {\n       \tif lowering.DiskStorePath == \"\" || scanSourceLimit <= 0 {\n       \t\treturn func() {}\n       \t}\n       \tif extract.PlanPartitions(paths, excludes, scanSourceLimit, scanSourceBudget) != nil {\n       \t\treturn func() {}\n       \t}\n       \tprev := lowering.UseIntStore\n       \tlowering.UseIntStore = true\n       \treturn func() { lowering.UseIntStore = prev }\n       }\n       ```\n     - Wiring in `scanPathsWithProfileDemand` (before `extract.BuildGraph`):\n       ```go\n       // The store choice is per build: a partitioned scan sets UseIntStore around its whole\n       // loop, and a run that must serialise one graph too big for the ceiling keeps the\n       // disk-backed store this scan was armed with.\n       restoreStore := holdOneGraphInRAM(paths, build.Excludes)\n       g, stats, err := extract.BuildGraph(paths, extract.SharedDeltaCache(), build)\n       restoreStore()\n       ```\n   - `cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go` — **MODIFIED (the tests)**: imports `+extract`, `+usg`; added:\n     - `TestBoundedOneGraphScanHoldsItsGraphInRAM` — arms `applyMaxRAM(\"8GB\")` (with `cacheHome(t)`, memory-limit save/restore), scans `partitionFixture(t, 3)` via `scanPathsWithProfileDemand(..., true, extract.Options{})`, asserts store is NOT `*usg.BadgerGraph` (with `t.Cleanup(func() { _ = usg.Close(g) })`). This FAILS on HEAD, PASSES with fix.\n     - `TestBoundedScanSpillsAGraphTheCeilingCannotHold` — squeezes `scanSourceLimit, scanSourceBudget = 1, 1` (saved/restored), asserts store IS `*usg.BadgerGraph`. Passes before and after (guards the disk store's role).\n   - Read for understanding (unmodified): `cmd/vyql/memwatch.go`, `cmd/vyql/graphstore.go` (uses os.UserCacheDir, NOT TMPDIR), `cmd/vyql/flags.go` (memprofile via onExit), `internal/extract/partition.go`, `internal/extract/pipeline.go`, `internal/usg/badgergraph.go`, `internal/usg/intstore.go`, `internal/extract/lowering/incremental.go`, `cmd/vyql/partition_test.go` (fixture/idioms), `cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go` (idioms).\n   - `CHANGELOG.md` — read header/format last (Keep-a-Changelog; latest `## [0.6.1] - 2026-09-11` has directly-related precedents); an entry is still to be added.\n   - `harness.err`, `harness.log` — untracked leftovers from the harness (present at start; not mine to commit).\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - `go build` first attempt exit 2: module downloads in progress; re-running the build succeeded.\n   - `/usr/bin/time` not available → measured peak RSS by sampling `/proc/<pid>/status` VmRSS in a loop; `bc` missing → used `$(date +%s)` arithmetic.\n   - `vyql graph -max-ram` → \"flag provided but not defined: -max-ram\" (graph subcommand lacks the flag); reran without it.\n   - TMPDIR trick did NOT disable the badger store (first attempt still died at 3.3GiB): `newGraphStoreDir` prefers `os.UserCacheDir()`. Fixed experiment with `HOME=/nonexistent-home XDG_CACHE_HOME=/tmp/ro_tmp/xdg TMPDIR=/tmp/ro_tmp` (read-only dirs) → fallback engaged → 4GB scan completed (the decisive experiment).\n   - `ps -o rss` showed 0 for nohup'd background processes → switched to pgrep/proc sampling and foreground runs.\n   - Full `cmd/vyql` suite failures (`TestShippedDefinitionCorpusIsV2Only`, one `TestVyqlSpecs/cve_rank1376` case) with `VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs`: pre-existing environment artifact — the outer defs checkout contains a duplicate `vyql/` subdir (\"duplicate v2 declaration\"); verified identical failures at HEAD; resolved for testing by using `VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql` → suite green.\n   - golangci-lint not installed → installed v2.12.1 via `go install` → `0 issues`.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Reproduced the gap exactly: openrazer whole-repo scan under 4GB dies at 3.3GiB in ~8s, exit 1, empty report; pylib+daemon+scripts (90 Python files, 1.29M-node additive graph) is the trigger; pairs are fine.\n   - Established root cause by measurement: lowering is NOT the problem (2s, additive node counts). The bounded route routes one-graph scans through the disk-backed BadgerGraph store, whose overhead peaks at 4626MiB where the in-RAM IntStore holds the same graph at 1220–1259MiB (3.8×); under the 4GB ceiling (stop at 3.5GB) the scan is killed during the bindings phase just before finishing.\n   - Fix: decide the store by the same affordability measure that decides partitioning — target inside the one-graph limit (`PlanPartitions(...) == nil`) → in-RAM int store; over the limit → disk store stays (and plain scans partition). Bonus: `-stats`/graph-json bounded runs of fitting targets now also complete.\n   - Verified end-to-end: mandated `campaign-scan` on the whole openrazer clone at fix 33aa7f07 → exit 3, 208 findings, 8s, peak 1341MiB (threshold 3328MiB); at parent 8f50fda → 208 findings, exactly one fingerprint differs (087c951d764434db → 2aa47a94d641bcfa); driver subtree alone → 105 findings, matching the rank's recorded base number (engine change preserves it).\n   - Test provenance: new test fails on HEAD, passes with fix (verified by swapping HEAD main.go in and out; `/tmp/main_fixed.go` backup already restored).\n   - Suites: cmd/vyql ok (108.6s), internal/usg + internal/extract + internal/extract/lowering ok, full `go test -count=1 ./...` exit 0 (30 ok).\n   - Identified an adjacent PRE-EXISTING issue (out of scope, verified identical at HEAD): a pathological synthetic fixture (12 files × 2000 same-named Python functions, 1.9MB) partitions into 3 under 4GB but a partition's lowering still hits the stop — a separate lowering-density (graph-per-byte) problem to be named in the verdict, not fixed here.\n   - Blast radius (for verdict): every bounded (`-max-ram`) single-graph scan changes store BadgerGraph → IntStore; unbounded scans code-path identical (helper no-ops when DiskStorePath==\"\"); partitioned scans unchanged (already int store); over-limit needsGraph runs keep the disk store; OWASP benchmarks run unbounded → unchanged; corpora not present in this environment so benchmarks were not run (to be stated honestly).\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The initial campaign task prompt (the only genuine user turn): \"# What every role obeys … You are one step of a campaign that adds CVE detections to a scanner … Stay inside the lane [Change only files under vyql/ — for the rank roles; engine role: only internal/, cmd/, go.mod, go.sum] … Use the commands rather than performing their steps [campaign-scan <target> --data-dir <vyql data dir>] … Say what you did, not what you intended [Every role ends by writing one file to $VERDICT_PATH … Silence is read as a failure] … Name a blocker for what it is … Your work counts only committed … Leftovers in your worktree are from a dead run [git reset --hard && git clean -fd safe only in your worktree] … # Closing an engine gap … The smallest change that makes the behaviour expressible … A Go test that fails without your change … Committed in the worktree you were given, and nowhere else … Blast radius: Say plainly in your answer which ranks the change affects … What you cannot do: You do not merge … three refusals of one tree … park the gap … The task is in /campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.task.json. Write the verdict to /campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.answer.json.\" (Accompanied by git status: branch `engine-work/the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan`, untracked harness.err/harness.log, and commit-attribution instructions: commits end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`.)\n   - The current summary request (no new task content).\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Add a CHANGELOG.md entry under a new `### Fixed` (Unreleased/new version per Keep-a-Changelog format used) describing the fix with the measured numbers.\n   - Commit the change in this worktree: `cmd/vyql/main.go`, `cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go`, `CHANGELOG.md`, message ending with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`.\n   - Write the verdict JSON to `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.answer.json` (files = the committed files; evidence = reproduction, measurements, failing-before test, mandated-scan results at both revisions; blast_radius = all bounded single-graph scans change store, unbounded/benchmark path identical; note the adjacent pre-existing partition-lowering density blowup and that OWASP corpora are absent so benchmarks were not runnable).\n   - Do NOT commit harness.err/harness.log (harness leftovers).\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before this summary I had finished all verification (full suite green, lint 0 issues, e2e mandated scans at both revisions, peak-RSS measurements, failing-before test proof, diff reviewed) and had just read the head of `CHANGELOG.md` to add an entry per AGENTS.md (\"Reasoning belongs in CHANGELOG.md and the pull request\"). The latest entry is:\n   ```\n   ## [0.6.1] - 2026-09-11\n   ### Fixed\n   - **A bounded scan of a dense-language target completes.** …\n   - **A partitioned scan holds each partition in RAM instead of routing it through the disk-backed graph store.** The disk store's write path — memtable arenas, SST builders, block cache — costs as much again as a partition's whole graph …\n   ```\n   The working tree currently holds: `M cmd/vyql/main.go` (+37/−4: holdOneGraphInRAM helper, wiring in scanPathsWithProfileDemand, applyMaxRAM comment), `M cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go` (+66: two new tests + imports), untracked `harness.err`/`harness.log`. Nothing committed yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Write the CHANGELOG.md entry (matching the 0.6.1 \"Fixed\" bullet style, with the measured figures: 4626MiB disk-store peak vs 1220MiB in-RAM on the same repository; whole-repo openrazer scan now 208 findings/8s/1341MiB peak under the mandated 4GB/180s), then `git add cmd/vyql/main.go cmd/vyql/maxram_test.go CHANGELOG.md` and commit with a message ending `Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>`, then write `/campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan.answer.json` — per the task's requirements: \"Every role ends by writing one file to `$VERDICT_PATH`\", \"Your work counts only committed … name in the verdict exactly the files your commits carry\", and \"Blast radius: Say plainly in your answer which ranks the change affects beyond the ones the gap lists.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /campaign/work/engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/.claude/projects/-campaign-work-engine-the-engine-s-memory-safety-stop-ends-a-whole-repository-scan/f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11.jsonl\nContinue the 