{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_d8520565ef22471ba5a9c3f1","type":"tool_result","content":"{\n  \"gap\": \"a-c-cast-expression-lowers-to-a-pass-through-nir-thru-that-d\",\n  \"status\": \"DONE\",\n  \"commit\": \"fed5075a6\",\n  \"commits\": [\n    \"fed5075a6\"\n  ],\n  \"branch\": \"engine-work/a-c-cast-expression-lowers-to-a-pass-through-nir-thru-that-d\",\n  \"base\": \"3aee370e5\",\n  \"changed_files\": [\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go\",\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c_test.go\"\n  ],\n  \"what_was_missing\": \"The C frontend erased an explicit conversion in both places it could have carried it. internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go, the shared `case \\\"parenthesized_expression\\\", \\\"cast_expression\\\"` arm of (*ccConv).expr, lowers a cast to nir.Thru{Inner: operand} -- a transparent wrapper with no room for a type -- and (*ccConv).ccExprShape returns the operand's shape for the same node, so `(int)x` and `x` produce the same NIR, the same shape token and the same node path. Nothing downstream can tell a size_t that was truncated to 32 bits from the size_t itself, so no binding can label the narrowing and no rule can condition on whether the value a bounds check compares, or a copy size carries, had already lost its high half.\\n\\nThe sibling spelling of the same weakness is a first-class engine fact: analysis.narrow_width.bounds_check (ccNarrowDeclaredBoundsCheckObservations, shipped for rank 1275) reports a guard written over two locals DECLARED at 32 bits, and vyql/bindings/c/narrow_declared_bounds_check.vyql turns it into code.OffsetLengthBoundsOverflow. The cast-narrowed spelling of the identical weakness had no fact at all, which is the asymmetry rank 2028's spec records in full (vyql/tests/cve003/cve_rank2028_libssh2_check_length_int_narrowing.test.vyql: \\\"Closing the family needs a narrow_cast.bounds_check observation beside narrow_width.bounds_check, reading the cast's target type and the operand's\\\"). That spec also measured why a data-layer workaround cannot substitute: a substring test on `<=(int)(` over the function-scope binary token fires on the vulnerable form, but the same text occurs 32 times across curl/redis/git/openssl and roughly two thirds of those are asserts, shift counts, sizeof-derived bounds and a double->int conversion -- the separating information is the operand's type, which only the frontend has.\\n\\nBlocked rank 2216 (brotli, CVE-2020-36846) is the copy-size half of the same gap: c/dec/decode.c CopyUncompressedBlockToOutput reads `int nbytes = (int)BrotliGetRemainingBytes(&s->br);`, clamps `nbytes` against two limits, and hands `(size_t)nbytes` to BrotliCopyBytes; the fix caps the size_t inside BrotliGetRemainingBytes. That rank's verdict names this gap first: \\\"the (int) truncation of BrotliGetRemainingBytes' size_t result is invisible to the engine (cast_expression lowers to nir.Thru), so no rule can condition on whether that value was capped before narrowing.\\\"\",\n  \"what_changed\": \"One new frontend observation in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go, additive, C/C++/ObjC only, called from the existing function_definition observation list beside ccNarrowDeclaredBoundsCheckObservations and inside the same !ccOWASPBenchmarkFastPath() guard.\\n\\nccNarrowingCastBoundsCheckObservations emits analysis.narrow_cast.bounds_check when a value the FILE states is wider than 32 bits is narrowed by an explicit cast to a 32-bit-or-narrower integer type and the narrowed value is what a relational comparison then reads. Const argument tokens carry the detail a binding needs: target=<cast spelling>, source=wide_declared|wide_result|wide_cast, origin=<the name or type that carries the width>, operand=<the operand as written, bounded at 96 chars>, read=cast_in_comparison|narrowed_local_compared, and dest=<local> for the second shape. The node is located at the cast itself, and sites are deduped by line.\\n\\nWidth comes from the translation unit and nowhere else:\\n  - ccWideDeclaredNames walks the parameter list and the body's declarations for names declared at one of the wide spellings (size_t, ssize_t, ptrdiff_t, off_t/off64_t/loff_t, uint64_t/int64_t/u_int64_t, uintmax_t/intmax_t, uintptr_t/intptr_t, the long and long long families). A pointer, array or function declarator is skipped however wide its element type -- the name holds an address, not the wide value.\\n  - ccWideReturningFunctions caches, per file, the names the file declares or defines with a wide return type (ccWideReturnDeclRe: type, name, then the parameter list's '('; a function returning a POINTER to a wide type does not match because the '*' sits between them).\\n  - ccWideValueOrigin decides what makes the cast's operand wide, following only the positions whose width the operand's own value carries -- parentheses, arithmetic and bitwise binary operators, arithmetic unary operators, both arms of a conditional, and an inner cast (a cast to a wide type IS the width, source=wide_cast). It stops at a subscript, a member selection, a dereference, an address-of and a call the file does not type, because the value there is an element, a field or a result whose width the name beside it does not state.\\n  - ccNarrowingCastSites carries two contexts down the CST: the arithmetic spine of a relational comparison (so `(int)(a-b) <= c` is a compared cast, while `<<`/`>>`, `&&`/`||` and `==`/`!=` are not comparisons for this purpose), and the name a DECLARATION or a plain `=` assignment binds the cast's value to. A compound assignment (`ix &= (uint32_t)mask`) does not bind: there the cast is an operand of the masking, not the value a later comparison reads. Every other position -- a call argument, a subscript key, an initializer element -- opens a fresh context.\\n  - ccComparedRelationally checks the compacted body for the bound local read as a relational operand, with identifier boundaries and with '<<'/'>>' excluded.\\nA cheap prefilter (ccHasNarrowCastText over the compacted body) skips the CST walk for the overwhelming majority of functions, which contain no cast to a narrow integer type at all.\\n\\nNothing existing was modified: (*ccConv).expr still lowers a cast to nir.Thru, ccExprShape still returns the operand's shape, no context token changed, no other frontend was touched, and nir gained no node.\",\n  \"test\": \"TestCNarrowingCastBoundsCheckObservation in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c_test.go, the package that changed, using the existing cFuncHasAnalysisToken helper and ExtractC. One fixture holds eleven functions.\\n\\nFires, with every token asserted:\\n  - vulnerable_narrowed_local -- rank 2216's shape: `int nbytes = (int)remaining_bytes(br);` with remaining_bytes declared `static size_t` in the same file, then `if (nbytes > limit)`. Asserts target=int, source=wide_result, origin=remaining_bytes, read=narrowed_local_compared, dest=nbytes.\\n  - vulnerable_widened_then_narrowed -- `int total = (int)((uint64_t)a + b);` compared afterwards: source=wide_cast, origin=uint64_t.\\n  - vulnerable_cast_in_comparison -- rank 2028's shape: `((int)(buf->len - len) <= (int)len)` with a size_t parameter: source=wide_declared, origin=len, read=cast_in_comparison, operand=(buf->len-len).\\nQuiet, asserted for both read= tokens: fixed_compared_at_width (rank 2028's actual fix, the remainder computed and compared at width), quiet_widening_cast, quiet_sizeof_bound `(int)(sizeof(name)-1)`, quiet_shift_count `(unsigned int)(bits & 7)` as a shift count, quiet_shifted_local (`nbytes >> 3` is not a bounds check), quiet_uncompared_local, quiet_pointer_to_wide (`size_t *lenp` is an address), quiet_untyped_callee (`(int)strlen(s)` -- strlen is not declared in this file), and the wide-returning helper itself.\\n\\nVerified RED before the change and green after: with internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go restored to 3aee370e5 and the test file left in place, it fails at `vulnerable_narrowed_local missing narrowing-cast bounds check token \\\"target=int\\\"` (the test names no new identifier, so it compiles against the pre-change tree). It also separates rank 2028's real pair as files: the vulnerable _libssh2_check_length reports misc.c:14 target=int source=wide_declared origin=len operand=(buf->len-len) read=cast_in_comparison, and the fixed revision reports nothing.\\n\\nSuite: VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql go test ./... -count=1 exits 0 over every package (this includes TestVyqlSpecs against the shipped definitions). gofmt -l clean over internal/ and cmd/; go vet clean on the changed package. Without $VYQL_HOME several packages panic on the missing data directory, which is pre-existing and unrelated.\",\n  \"verification\": \"campaign-scan (timeout 180, --max-ram 4GB, --cache off) against /campaign/repos/defs/vyql, comparing a binary built at branch base 3aee370e5 with one built at HEAD, over three C checkouts already on this machine:\\n  - brotli (rank 2216's clone, all of c/, 2218 findings): output BYTE-IDENTICAL before and after.\\n  - haproxy (16149 findings): every finding line -- rule, severity, confidence, fingerprint, location, concept, control -- identical. 1096 lines differ, all of them `taint path:` renderings: node ids shift by the added statements, and on some paths an equally-ranked witness is printed instead (_51d_fetch vs _51d_conv through the same source and sink).\\n  - freeradius (6803 findings): same picture -- 798 taint-path lines, plus 6 `unless path coveredBy core.ZeroValueExclusion` diagnostics whose sibling-path list is the same SET in a different order (checked programmatically). No finding, count or fingerprint moved.\\nScan time unchanged within run-to-run noise: freeradius 6.4s both binaries on interleaved trials; micropython (2038 C files) base 22.0/16.3s, HEAD 18.5/22.9s.\\n\\nHow often the fact fires, counted by extracting each tree and collecting the emitted statements: brotli 1 site / 93 files, haproxy 5 / 475, freeradius 4 / 323, msquic 2 / 539, micropython 2 / 2038, fontforge 1 / 455, irssi 0 / 322, fluidsynth 0 / 167, pacemaker 0 / 222, libsolv 0 / 198, net-snmp 39 / 1389. net-snmp is the densest and every site there is a true instance of the class -- `if ((int) pkt_len <= len_len)` in asn_parse_nlength, `i * 4 < (int) buflen` in md5.c's MDget, `i < (int) idlen` in snmpusm.c -- a size_t compared at 32 bits. Whether any of them is exploitable is the rule's question, which is the layer split this keeps.\\n\\nNo shipped binding reads analysis.narrow_cast.bounds_check, so nothing is labelled and no finding moves until a rank writes one; the scans above are the evidence for that.\",\n  \"blast_radius\": \"Beyond the listed rank 2216, the change is visible to:\\n  - rank 2028 (libssh2, CVE-2019-13115, currently ATTENTION with this gap named in its spec) -- the same family, and the shape its spec asked for is exactly what now fires. Its spec header and its verify_current_expected line become stale once a binding reads the fact; that edit is that rank's, not mine.\\n  - every rank whose clone is C, C++ or ObjC, in two ways. First, the observation adds statements to function bodies, which renumbers graph nodes: findings and fingerprints are stable (measured on three trees) but printed taint paths shift and, where several equal-length witnesses exist, a different one may be printed. Any rank whose spec or verdict quotes a taint path verbatim will see that text move. Second, once a rank writes a binding over the new fact, that binding's concept and rule apply corpus-wide, and net-snmp shows the density to expect (39 sites in 1389 files) -- the judgement about which of those is a finding belongs in the rule, not here.\\n  - no other language. The observation is emitted only by the C-family frontend, no nir node or lowering path changed, and the OWASP Java/Python/other-port benchmarks cannot reach it (they were not run: neither corpus is on this machine, and a C-frontend-only addition has no route into them).\\nThe campaign should still re-measure the span, because node renumbering touches every C tree in it.\",\n  \"considered_and_rejected\": [\n    \"Carrying the width in NIR -- a new nir.Cast node, or a Type field on nir.Thru. It is the literal reading of the gap sentence and it is much wider: Thru is emitted by fifteen frontends, the node set is gob-registered for the parse cache and the incremental delta cache, and every switch over nir.Expr in lowering, parsecache and the frontends would have to learn the new shape. Worse, it would not by itself close the gap: bindings match node paths, analysis facts and context tokens, so a type sitting on a wrapper the lowering deliberately makes transparent is still invisible to every rule. The width has to reach the layer above as a fact, and the frontend is where the declared types are.\",\n    \"Lowering a cast to a synthetic call, `__cast.int(x)`, in the style of the existing `__deref`. That does surface the target width as a node path bindings can match, and bindings do match __deref today. Rejected on blast radius: casts are everywhere in C, so it adds a node and an argument slot to a large fraction of all C expressions, changes the shape of taint paths through every cast, and hands the noise problem rank 2028 measured (asserts, shift counts, sizeof bounds, double->int) straight to the data layer with no type information attached.\",\n    \"Making ccExprShape render the cast, so `assign_shape`/`binary_shape`/`call_arg_shape` carry `(int)...`. Two lines of code, but it REWRITES existing context tokens: any shipped binding matching a shape token whose expression happens to contain a cast would stop matching, silently, corpus-wide. An additive `cast:` token would avoid that, but a token is text: it cannot say the operand was a size_t, which is the one thing the data layer was missing.\",\n    \"Emitting a second fact for the copy-size use (`analysis.narrow_cast.size_use`), since the gap sentence names \\\"a bounds check OR copy-size use\\\". Rank 2216's own site does both -- it compares the narrowed nbytes twice before passing it to BrotliCopyBytes -- so the comparison fact already reaches it, and rank 2028 needs only the comparison. A rank that wants the copy can pair the fact's dest= token with the call_arg tokens the function scope already carries. Naming a set of copy/allocation APIs in the frontend would also be library knowledge in the engine, which is a binding's job.\",\n    \"Typing a callee's return across files, which is what brotli's real decode.c needs (BrotliGetRemainingBytes is declared in c/dec/bit_reader.h). The C frontend converts one file per worker with no cross-file pass; adding one means a pre-scan phase and shared state in a parallel pipeline used by C, C++ and ObjC. That is a second gap, not this one, and it is stated as a residual instead.\",\n    \"Suppressing a narrowing cast written inside assert(), which rank 2028's noise study counted as 8 of 32 substring hits. Under NDEBUG such a check bounds nothing, so reporting it states something true; and deciding that an assert does not count is judgement, which belongs in the rule that reads the fact.\",\n    \"Requiring the comparison to appear after the narrowing in source order for the narrowed_local shape. The existing narrow_width fact is function-scoped in the same way, and the ordering would need offsets the compacted text does not carry back to node positions. Restricting the binding to a plain `=` assignment removed the one real mis-linkage this caused (brotli's `prev_ix &= (uint32_t)ring_buffer_mask` beside an earlier `if (prev_ix < cur_ix)`), which is why that guard is in.\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewer_should_know\": \"What is closed: the C frontend can now state that a value it knows is wider than 32 bits was truncated by a cast, and that a bounds check reads the truncated value. That is the behaviour the gap names, and it is what rank 2028's spec asked for by name.\\n\\nWhat this does NOT do for rank 2216, stated plainly. Two things stand between the fact and a FIXED verdict there, and neither is this gap:\\n  1. Cross-file typing. brotli's narrowing sits in c/dec/decode.c while BrotliGetRemainingBytes is declared `static BROTLI_INLINE size_t` in c/dec/bit_reader.h, so the file the cast is read in does not state the width and no fact is emitted at that site (confirmed: 1 site in the whole brotli checkout, in c/enc). The same code with both functions in one file -- how a spec test is written, and how the Go test exercises it -- does emit.\\n  2. Revision discrimination. The fix commit 223d80cf caps the size_t INSIDE BrotliGetRemainingBytes in the header; decode.c is byte-identical across the two revisions. No fact computed from decode.c can separate them, so closing this gap alone will not flip rank 2216 -- it would need the callee's cap to be visible where the narrowing is judged. That rank's verdict also records a second, independent blocker of its own (the br->avail_in struct-field store the C frontend drops, ranks 1204/1794).\\nRank 2028 IS separated by this change end to end: its vulnerable function emits the fact, its fix does not.\\n\\nResiduals worth a reviewer's eye:\\n  - `long` is treated as wide, which is right on LP64 and wrong on Windows LLP64; a `(int)` of a long there is not a narrowing. The fact says the conversion happened, and the rule weighs it.\\n  - Typedef aliases for wide types (`typedef uint64_t u64;`) are not resolved -- only the standard spellings are. The narrow_width fact has the same limit.\\n  - A struct member or an array element is never typed, so `(int)(buf->dataptr - buf->data)` -- the FIRST of rank 2028's two casts -- is not what fires; the second one, over the size_t parameter, is.\\n  - The narrowed-local shape is function-scoped, so a comparison of the same name elsewhere in the function satisfies it wherever it sits relative to the cast.\"\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f1b7e732-1060-4c03-a560-f041798bec11","uuid":"743c7d18-a804-480b-ac6d-e55922040b45","timestamp":"2026-09-16T23:10:29.520Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"{\n  \"gap\": \"a-c-cast-expression-lowers-to-a-pass-through-nir-thru-that-d\",\n  \"status\": \"DONE\",\n  \"commit\": \"fed5075a6\",\n  \"commits\": [\n    \"fed5075a6\"\n  ],\n  \"branch\": \"engine-work/a-c-cast-expression-lowers-to-a-pass-through-nir-thru-that-d\",\n  \"base\": \"3aee370e5\",\n  \"changed_files\": [\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go\",\n    \"internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c_test.go\"\n  ],\n  \"what_was_missing\": \"The C frontend erased an explicit conversion in both places it could have carried it. internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go, the shared `case \\\"parenthesized_expression\\\", \\\"cast_expression\\\"` arm of (*ccConv).expr, lowers a cast to nir.Thru{Inner: operand} -- a transparent wrapper with no room for a type -- and (*ccConv).ccExprShape returns the operand's shape for the same node, so `(int)x` and `x` produce the same NIR, the same shape token and the same node path. Nothing downstream can tell a size_t that was truncated to 32 bits from the size_t itself, so no binding can label the narrowing and no rule can condition on whether the value a bounds check compares, or a copy size carries, had already lost its high half.\\n\\nThe sibling spelling of the same weakness is a first-class engine fact: analysis.narrow_width.bounds_check (ccNarrowDeclaredBoundsCheckObservations, shipped for rank 1275) reports a guard written over two locals DECLARED at 32 bits, and vyql/bindings/c/narrow_declared_bounds_check.vyql turns it into code.OffsetLengthBoundsOverflow. The cast-narrowed spelling of the identical weakness had no fact at all, which is the asymmetry rank 2028's spec records in full (vyql/tests/cve003/cve_rank2028_libssh2_check_length_int_narrowing.test.vyql: \\\"Closing the family needs a narrow_cast.bounds_check observation beside narrow_width.bounds_check, reading the cast's target type and the operand's\\\"). That spec also measured why a data-layer workaround cannot substitute: a substring test on `<=(int)(` over the function-scope binary token fires on the vulnerable form, but the same text occurs 32 times across curl/redis/git/openssl and roughly two thirds of those are asserts, shift counts, sizeof-derived bounds and a double->int conversion -- the separating information is the operand's type, which only the frontend has.\\n\\nBlocked rank 2216 (brotli, CVE-2020-36846) is the copy-size half of the same gap: c/dec/decode.c CopyUncompressedBlockToOutput reads `int nbytes = (int)BrotliGetRemainingBytes(&s->br);`, clamps `nbytes` against two limits, and hands `(size_t)nbytes` to BrotliCopyBytes; the fix caps the size_t inside BrotliGetRemainingBytes. That rank's verdict names this gap first: \\\"the (int) truncation of BrotliGetRemainingBytes' size_t result is invisible to the engine (cast_expression lowers to nir.Thru), so no rule can condition on whether that value was capped before narrowing.\\\"\",\n  \"what_changed\": \"One new frontend observation in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go, additive, C/C++/ObjC only, called from the existing function_definition observation list beside ccNarrowDeclaredBoundsCheckObservations and inside the same !ccOWASPBenchmarkFastPath() guard.\\n\\nccNarrowingCastBoundsCheckObservations emits analysis.narrow_cast.bounds_check when a value the FILE states is wider than 32 bits is narrowed by an explicit cast to a 32-bit-or-narrower integer type and the narrowed value is what a relational comparison then reads. Const argument tokens carry the detail a binding needs: target=<cast spelling>, source=wide_declared|wide_result|wide_cast, origin=<the name or type that carries the width>, operand=<the operand as written, bounded at 96 chars>, read=cast_in_comparison|narrowed_local_compared, and dest=<local> for the second shape. The node is located at the cast itself, and sites are deduped by line.\\n\\nWidth comes from the translation unit and nowhere else:\\n  - ccWideDeclaredNames walks the parameter list and the body's declarations for names declared at one of the wide spellings (size_t, ssize_t, ptrdiff_t, off_t/off64_t/loff_t, uint64_t/int64_t/u_int64_t, uintmax_t/intmax_t, uintptr_t/intptr_t, the long and long long families). A pointer, array or function declarator is skipped however wide its element type -- the name holds an address, not the wide value.\\n  - ccWideReturningFunctions caches, per file, the names the file declares or defines with a wide return type (ccWideReturnDeclRe: type, name, then the parameter list's '('; a function returning a POINTER to a wide type does not match because the '*' sits between them).\\n  - ccWideValueOrigin decides what makes the cast's operand wide, following only the positions whose width the operand's own value carries -- parentheses, arithmetic and bitwise binary operators, arithmetic unary operators, both arms of a conditional, and an inner cast (a cast to a wide type IS the width, source=wide_cast). It stops at a subscript, a member selection, a dereference, an address-of and a call the file does not type, because the value there is an element, a field or a result whose width the name beside it does not state.\\n  - ccNarrowingCastSites carries two contexts down the CST: the arithmetic spine of a relational comparison (so `(int)(a-b) <= c` is a compared cast, while `<<`/`>>`, `&&`/`||` and `==`/`!=` are not comparisons for this purpose), and the name a DECLARATION or a plain `=` assignment binds the cast's value to. A compound assignment (`ix &= (uint32_t)mask`) does not bind: there the cast is an operand of the masking, not the value a later comparison reads. Every other position -- a call argument, a subscript key, an initializer element -- opens a fresh context.\\n  - ccComparedRelationally checks the compacted body for the bound local read as a relational operand, with identifier boundaries and with '<<'/'>>' excluded.\\nA cheap prefilter (ccHasNarrowCastText over the compacted body) skips the CST walk for the overwhelming majority of functions, which contain no cast to a narrow integer type at all.\\n\\nNothing existing was modified: (*ccConv).expr still lowers a cast to nir.Thru, ccExprShape still returns the operand's shape, no context token changed, no other frontend was touched, and nir gained no node.\",\n  \"test\": \"TestCNarrowingCastBoundsCheckObservation in internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c_test.go, the package that changed, using the existing cFuncHasAnalysisToken helper and ExtractC. One fixture holds eleven functions.\\n\\nFires, with every token asserted:\\n  - vulnerable_narrowed_local -- rank 2216's shape: `int nbytes = (int)remaining_bytes(br);` with remaining_bytes declared `static size_t` in the same file, then `if (nbytes > limit)`. Asserts target=int, source=wide_result, origin=remaining_bytes, read=narrowed_local_compared, dest=nbytes.\\n  - vulnerable_widened_then_narrowed -- `int total = (int)((uint64_t)a + b);` compared afterwards: source=wide_cast, origin=uint64_t.\\n  - vulnerable_cast_in_comparison -- rank 2028's shape: `((int)(buf->len - len) <= (int)len)` with a size_t parameter: source=wide_declared, origin=len, read=cast_in_comparison, operand=(buf->len-len).\\nQuiet, asserted for both read= tokens: fixed_compared_at_width (rank 2028's actual fix, the remainder computed and compared at width), quiet_widening_cast, quiet_sizeof_bound `(int)(sizeof(name)-1)`, quiet_shift_count `(unsigned int)(bits & 7)` as a shift count, quiet_shifted_local (`nbytes >> 3` is not a bounds check), quiet_uncompared_local, quiet_pointer_to_wide (`size_t *lenp` is an address), quiet_untyped_callee (`(int)strlen(s)` -- strlen is not declared in this file), and the wide-returning helper itself.\\n\\nVerified RED before the change and green after: with internal/extract/frontend/treesitter/c.go restored to 3aee370e5 and the test file left in place, it fails at `vulnerable_narrowed_local missing narrowing-cast bounds check token \\\"target=int\\\"` (the test names no new identifier, so it compiles against the pre-change tree). It also separates rank 2028's real pair as files: the vulnerable _libssh2_check_length reports misc.c:14 target=int source=wide_declared origin=len operand=(buf->len-len) read=cast_in_comparison, and the fixed revision reports nothing.\\n\\nSuite: VYQL_HOME=/campaign/repos/defs/vyql go test ./... -count=1 exits 0 over every package (this includes TestVyqlSpecs against the shipped definitions). gofmt -l clean over internal/ and cmd/; go vet clean on the changed package. Without $VYQL_HOME several packages panic on the missing data directory, which is pre-existing and unrelated.\",\n  \"verification\": \"campaign-scan (timeout 180, --max-ram 4GB, --cache off) against /campaign/repos/defs/vyql, comparing a binary built at branch base 3aee370e5 with one built at HEAD, over three C checkouts already on this machine:\\n  - brotli (rank 2216's clone, all of c/, 2218 findings): output BYTE-IDENTICAL before and after.\\n  - haproxy (16149 findings): every finding line -- rule, severity, confidence, fingerprint, location, concept, control -- identical. 1096 lines differ, all of them `taint path:` renderings: node ids shift by the added statements, and on some paths an equally-ranked witness is printed instead (_51d_fetch vs _51d_conv through the same source and sink).\\n  - freeradius (6803 findings): same picture -- 798 taint-path lines, plus 6 `unless path coveredBy core.ZeroValueExclusion` diagnostics whose sibling-path list is the same SET in a different order (checked programmatically). No finding, count or fingerprint moved.\\nScan time unchanged within run-to-run noise: freeradius 6.4s both binaries on interleaved trials; micropython (2038 C files) base 22.0/16.3s, HEAD 18.5/22.9s.\\n\\nHow often the fact fires, counted by extracting each tree and collecting the emitted statements: brotli 1 site / 93 files, haproxy 5 / 475, freeradius 4 / 323, msquic 2 / 539, micropython 2 / 2038, fontforge 1 / 455, irssi 0 / 322, fluidsynth 0 / 167, pacemaker 0 / 222, libsolv 0 / 198, net-snmp 39 / 1389. net-snmp is the densest and every site there is a true instance of the class -- `if ((int) pkt_len <= len_len)` in asn_parse_nlength, `i * 4 < (int) buflen` in md5.c's MDget, `i < (int) idlen` in snmpusm.c -- a size_t compared at 32 bits. Whether any of them is exploitable is the rule's question, which is the layer split this keeps.\\n\\nNo shipped binding reads analysis.narrow_cast.bounds_check, so nothing is labelled and no finding moves until a rank writes one; the scans above are the evidence for that.\",\n  \"blast_radius\": \"Beyond the listed rank 2216, the change is visible to:\\n  - rank 2028 (libssh2, CVE-2019-13115, currently ATTENTION with this gap named in its spec) -- the same family, and the shape its spec asked for is exactly what now fires. Its spec header and its verify_current_expected line become stale once a binding reads the fact; that edit is that rank's, not mine.\\n  - every rank whose clone is C, C++ or ObjC, in two ways. First, the observation adds statements to function bodies, which renumbers graph nodes: findings and fingerprints are stable (measured on three trees) but printed taint paths shift and, where several equal-length witnesses exist, a different one may be printed. Any rank whose spec or verdict quotes a taint path verbatim will see that text move. Second, once a rank writes a binding over the new fact, that binding's concept and rule apply corpus-wide, and net-snmp shows the density to expect (39 sites in 1389 files) -- the judgement about which of those is a finding belongs in the rule, not here.\\n  - no other language. The observation is emitted only by the C-family frontend, no nir node or lowering path changed, and the OWASP Java/Python/other-port benchmarks cannot reach it (they were not run: neither corpus is on this machine, and a C-frontend-only addition has no route into them).\\nThe campaign should still re-measure the span, because node renumbering touches every C tree in it.\",\n  \"considered_and_rejected\": [\n    \"Carrying the width in NIR -- a new nir.Cast node, or a Type field on nir.Thru. It is the literal reading of the gap sentence and it is much wider: Thru is emitted by fifteen frontends, the node set is gob-registered for the parse cache and the incremental delta cache, and every switch over nir.Expr in lowering, parsecache and the frontends would have to learn the new shape. Worse, it would not by itself close the gap: bindings match node paths, analysis facts and context tokens, so a type sitting on a wrapper the lowering deliberately makes transparent is still invisible to every rule. The width has to reach the layer above as a fact, and the frontend is where the declared types are.\",\n    \"Lowering a cast to a synthetic call, `__cast.int(x)`, in the style of the existing `__deref`. That does surface the target width as a node path bindings can match, and bindings do match __deref today. Rejected on blast radius: casts are everywhere in C, so it adds a node and an argument slot to a large fraction of all C expressions, changes the shape of taint paths through every cast, and hands the noise problem rank 2028 measured (asserts, shift counts, sizeof bounds, double->int) straight to the data layer with no type information attached.\",\n    \"Making ccExprShape render the cast, so `assign_shape`/`binary_shape`/`call_arg_shape` carry `(int)...`. Two lines of code, but it REWRITES existing context tokens: any shipped binding matching a shape token whose expression happens to contain a cast would stop matching, silently, corpus-wide. An additive `cast:` token would avoid that, but a token is text: it cannot say the operand was a size_t, which is the one thing the data layer was missing.\",\n    \"Emitting a second fact for the copy-size use (`analysis.narrow_cast.size_use`), since the gap sentence names \\\"a bounds check OR copy-size use\\\". Rank 2216's own site does both -- it compares the narrowed nbytes twice before passing it to BrotliCopyBytes -- so the comparison fact already reaches it, and rank 2028 needs only the comparison. A rank that wants the copy can pair the fact's dest= token with the call_arg tokens the function scope already carries. Naming a set of copy/allocation APIs in the frontend would also be library knowledge in the engine, which is a binding's job.\",\n    \"Typing a callee's return across files, which is what brotli's real decode.c needs (BrotliGetRemainingBytes is declared in c/dec/bit_reader.h). The C frontend converts one file per worker with no cross-file pass; adding one means a pre-scan phase and shared state in a parallel pipeline used by C, C++ and ObjC. That is a second gap, not this one, and it is stated as a residual instead.\",\n    \"Suppressing a narrowing cast written inside assert(), which rank 2028's noise study counted as 8 of 32 substring hits. Under NDEBUG such a check bounds nothing, so reporting it states something true; and deciding that an assert does not count is judgement, which belongs in the rule that reads the fact.\",\n    \"Requiring the comparison to appear after the narrowing in source order for the narrowed_local shape. The existing narrow_width fact is function-scoped in the same way, and the ordering would need offsets the compacted text does not carry back to node positions. Restricting the binding to a plain `=` assignment removed the one real mis-linkage this caused (brotli's `prev_ix &= (uint32_t)ring_buffer_mask` beside an earlier `if (prev_ix < cur_ix)`), which is why that guard is in.\"\n  ],\n  \"reviewer_should_know\": \"What is closed: the C frontend can now state that a value it knows is wider than 32 bits was truncated by a cast, and that a bounds check reads the truncated value. That is the behaviour the gap names, and it is what rank 2028's spec asked for by name.\\n\\nWhat this does NOT do for rank 2216, stated plainly. Two things stand between the fact and a FIXED verdict there, and neither is this gap:\\n  1. Cross-file typing. brotli's narrowing sits in c/dec/decode.c while BrotliGetRemainingBytes is declared `static BROTLI_INLINE size_t` in c/dec/bit_reader.h, so the file the cast is read in does not state the width and no fact is emitted at that site (confirmed: 1 site in the whole brotli checkout, in c/enc). The same code with both functions in one file -- how a spec test is written, and how the Go test exercises it -- does emit.\\n  2. Revision discrimination. The fix commit 223d80cf caps the size_t INSIDE BrotliGetRemainingBytes in the header; decode.c is byte-identical across the two revisions. No fact computed from decode.c can separate them, so closing this gap alone will not flip rank 2216 -- it would need the callee's cap to be visible where the narrowing is judged. That rank's verdict also records a second, independent blocker of its own (the br->avail_in struct-field store the C frontend drops, ranks 1204/1794).\\nRank 2028 IS separated by this change end to end: its vulnerable function emits the fact, its fix does not.\\n\\nResiduals worth a reviewer's eye:\\n  - `long` is treated as wide, which is right on LP64 and wrong on Windows LLP64; a `(int)` of a long there is not a narrowing. The fact says the conversion happened, and the rule weighs it.\\n  - Typedef aliases for wide types (`typedef uint64_t u64;`) are not resolved -- only the standard spellings are. The narrow_width fact has the same limit.\\n  - A struct member or an array element is never typed, so `(int)(buf->dataptr - buf->data)` -- the FIRST of rank 2028's two casts -- is not what fires; the second one, over the size_t parameter, is.\\n  - The narrowed-local shape is function-scoped, so a comparison of the same name elsewhere in the function satisfies it wherever it sits relative to the cast.\"\n}","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
